The gh-821 suite has suite-local helpers (`runsCli`, `oldRun`, `dispatched`) defined at the top of the suite callback — suite-scoped named FunctionDeclarations. The throwing-dispatch test is in the same suite (line 5153). So the natural pattern: add a suite-local helper next to `oldRun`/`runsCli`, e.g.:

```js
// gh-1107 CI follow-up: the head_sha matcher for the sweep CLI fake,
// extracted so the throwing-dispatch closure stays CC ≤ 8 (crap4js
// ratchet — the closure was grandfathered at 9 only by its old
// positional key; new keys must sit at or under the threshold).
function sweepRunsForHead(cmd, headSha) {
   var m = /head_sha=([^&"]+)/.exec(cmd);
   return m !== null && m[1] === headSha;
}
``

